Reliability review fixes (both MAJORs are in the extraction code, same region):

- MAJOR: per-USER cache dir (%LOCALAPPDATA% / $XDG_CACHE_HOME|~/.cache, 0o700)
  instead of world-writable os.tmpdir() — closes a local pre-plant attack where
  an attacker seeds forge-assets-<v>/ with a valid sentinel + malicious hooks.
- MAJOR: atomic + concurrency-safe extraction — write files+sentinel into a
  private mkdtemp sibling, then renameSync into the final path in one step; on
  EEXIST adopt the winner and discard ours. No rmSync of a dir another process
  reads; a half-written temp never gets the final name.
- Hardening: replace the near-tautological count assertion with a stat-check
  (each expected relpath exists + non-empty, lists any missing).
- Hardening: reject manifest keys that are absolute or contain '..' before write.
- Fix inaccurate bin/forge.js docs comment (TOOLCHAIN/VALIDATION aren't on disk).

Re-proven in a real compiled binary: extracts to %LOCALAPPDATA%\forge\assets-<v>,
142 assets, nested paths intact, sentinel present, idempotent. npm channel
unchanged (15 unit+drift, 105 regression green, eslint clean).

Follow-ups filed: bc92ba7a (drift vs generated artifact → step-3 f13b5073),
7f627647 (dev-version stale reuse), 7a584ad4 (narrow ASSET_ROOTS scripts bloat).

Issue: 9460dda1-2e69-4390-8f57-c62462118407

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
